paths tools/fixtures/a/aurora_file_placement_scan.sh tools/fixtures/a/aurora_file_placement_control.sh tools/a/aurora_file_placement_witness.rish active-designing/20260910-060204_the-bounded-torus-moonshots.md
what My own last lap's paper names its weakest joint in its own words: the two-thirds structure-drift tolerance is BORROWED from the room-granularity sibling rather than re-measured at file granularity. aurora_placement_scan.sh emits proxy_survives_structure_drift_upto_pct=60 over 67 room pairs; the file reading stands on 7,549 edges over 1,561 files and keeps only 0.2184 of them on-node against the room layout's 0.8463, so the margin above chance is thinner by construction and the borrowed number may not survive the finer unit at all. This lap re-measures it in the file scan rather than citing it: rewire a rising share of edges to random endpoints, re-run the same capacity-constrained greedy placement on the perturbed graph, score the resulting seating against the TRUE graph, and compare to the count-matched floor the scan already computes -- the sibling's own method, on this lane's own corpus. The prediction, stated before the run so it can be wrong: the file tolerance reads BELOW 60 percent, because a layout keeping a fifth of its edges on-node has less headroom to spend than one keeping four fifths. Falsifier named: if it reads at or above 60 the borrowing was sound and the paper's weakest joint closes in the paper's favor. Touches the three instruments this lane built yesterday, all of which exist and are rostered, plus row 7 of the moonshots page for a fourth erratum. No ledger row, no ceiling any peer watches, no module source, no peer-claimed file.
